            <ArticleTitle>Coronary obstruction by a calcific pericardial ring.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>595-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We report the unique case of a 62-year-old man whose left anterior descending artery was intermittently obstructed by a heavily calcified pericardial ring. This is a rare case in which a coronary artery has been compressed because of constrictive pericarditis.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
